cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "LiouScope: Multi-Diagnostic Relaxation Analysis for Open Quantum Lattice Systems"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Coworker Research"
version: "0.4.0"
date-released: "2026-06-07"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/marcohost33-maker/Liouscope"
url: "https://github.com/marcohost33-maker/Liouscope"
abstract: >-
  LiouScope is an open-source diagnostic framework for time-homogeneous
  Markovian open quantum systems described by Gorini-Kossakowski-Sudarshan-
  Lindblad (GKSL) generators. It quantifies when and why the Liouvillian gap
  fails as a relaxation-time predictor, providing 24 diagnostics (D1-D24;
  D1-D20 are the original submission set and D21-D24 are post-submission
  additions) organised in six layers (Spectral, Non-normality, Relaxation,
  Uncertainty, Classification, Governance) and a twelve-class mechanism
  taxonomy A1-A12.
keywords:
  - open quantum systems
  - Lindblad
  - Liouvillian gap
  - Mpemba effect
  - non-normal dynamics
  - pseudospectrum
  - quantum relaxation
